  "observation": "Two disjoint original trace windows of the field 23 entry-dialogue route capture 29993 complete batches and 73257 post-handler decisions. Reconstructed stage ordering, loop counters, budgets and all 40 captured global bytes match original execution. The 25 initialization batches use budget 65535 and mode zero; 29968 ordinary batches use budget eight and mode one. Observed returns comprise 29256 honored breaks, 736 exhausted budgets and one hard-dispatch safeguard. In 993 initialization handler returns, break requested remains one while execution continues. The first actor-zero batch runs 1025 handlers across frontend runs 510 and 511.",
  "interpretation": "Budget mode and exact break-flag comparisons govern batching. Initialization may keep executing a yielding instruction until the hard dispatch cap; it cannot be represented by a universal break-on-yield rule. The analysis reconstruction separates this policy from handler effects, which remain opaque original inputs for this comparison. These findings constrain future native timing and scenario initialization without assigning a tick rate or player-readiness meaning to raw globals.",
